    "title": "Euphemisms and Softened Language",
    "title_ko": "완곡어법",
    "focus_axis": "vocabulary"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Euphemisms soften uncomfortable topics: 'let go' (fired), 'pass away' (died), 'between jobs' (unemployed), 'downsizing' (layoffs). Recognizing and using these appropriately is a mark of social and professional fluency.",
    "explanation_ko": "완곡어법은 불편한 주제를 부드럽게 만듭니다: 'let go'(해고됨), 'pass away'(사망함), 'between jobs'(실직 중), 'downsizing'(정리해고). 이를 알아보고 적절히 쓰는 것은 사회적·직업적 유창함의 표시입니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "He was let go last month.",
        "ko": "그는 지난달에 해고됐어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "My grandfather passed away peacefully.",
        "ko": "제 할아버지는 편안히 돌아가셨어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "I'm currently between jobs.",
        "ko": "저는 지금 잠시 쉬고 있어요(실직 중)."
      }
    ]
  },
